// THE SHIP'S FOOD STORES (increment 3 of docs/design/ship-homes-and-logistics.md; the relay's
// src/relay/handlers/ship_stores.rs). Read by the relay at startup, disk first, the copy built
// into the exe only when this file is missing.
//
// The operator decided on 2026-10-04 (that design's open question 12): NPCs eat from the same
// food stores as players, and NPC homesteads mostly provide for themselves. So each store here
// is ONE stock of meals that everyone eats from: a crew member who eats takes one at the end of
// its meal in the mess hall (data/npc/chores.ron, `meal: true`), and a player takes one with
// the `take_meal` action on the store (the game's own hunger does not read it yet; serving
// meals into the food system is the design's increment 6).
//
// Every number below is a game default chosen for this increment, NOT a sourced figure.
//
//   stores        one row per store: id, label, the room it stands in (`place`, a room id of the
//                 relay's world), where in that room (`spot`, room-local x and z metres, like a
//                 chore's), the meals a new world starts with, and the most it holds.
//   meal_interval_hours
//                 hours of the relay's clock (real time) between one person's meals: 8 is three
//                 a day.
//   empty_store_retry_minutes
//                 how soon a crew member who found the store empty comes back to try again.
//   ship_farms_meals_per_day
//                 what fills the stores today: a stand-in for the ship's farms (the agricultural
//                 bay, the Commons garden) until goods are really carried aboard (the design's
//                 increment 9, shipments). Players put nothing in yet. 18 a day feeds the five
//                 crew who eat (15 a day at three meals each) with a little over for players.
//   npc_homestead_self_provided
//                 the operator's "NPC homesteads should mostly provide for themselves": the share
//                 of an NPC homestead household's meals its own homestead grows (crew.ron
//                 `household: "homestead"`); the rest come from these stores. 0.8 is "mostly".
//                 No shipped NPC lives on a homestead yet, so this waits for the first ones.
//   npc_homestead_fleet_meals_per_day
//                 OPEN QUESTION FOR THE OPERATOR (not decided here): how much an NPC homestead
//                 gives the fleet's stores, balanced against what human players give. Meals a
//                 day that EACH NPC homestead household puts into these stores. 0.0 is a
//                 placeholder that means "nothing until he decides"; like the share above it
//                 changes nothing until an NPC lives on a homestead.
(
    stores: [
        (
            id: "mess-hall-stores",
            label: "The mess hall's stores",
            place: "mess-hall",
            spot: (2.0, 2.0),
            meals: 90.0,
            capacity: 300.0,
        ),
    ],
    meal_interval_hours: 8.0,
    empty_store_retry_minutes: 30.0,
    ship_farms_meals_per_day: 18.0,
    npc_homestead_self_provided: 0.8,
    npc_homestead_fleet_meals_per_day: 0.0,
)
